WEBVTT

00:00:00.698 --> 00:00:02.298
Rhetorical synthesis.

00:00:02.298 --> 00:00:03.683
Read the goal first.

00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:05.139
The notes come last.

00:00:06.702 --> 00:00:08.377
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:10.562
A bulleted list of a student's notes.

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:13.455
And a question that says: the student wants to.

00:00:14.489 --> 00:00:18.878
It's testing whether you can choose information to do one specific job.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:21.181
Here's the method.

00:00:21.181 --> 00:00:22.956
Read the question first.

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.656
Skip the notes for now.

00:00:24.656 --> 00:00:27.886
Underline the goal: the action, and what it's about.

00:00:27.886 --> 00:00:29.561
Turn it into a checklist.

00:00:29.561 --> 00:00:32.461
Then pick the one choice that ticks every box.

00:00:32.461 --> 00:00:33.947
You barely need the notes.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.485
Know your goal words.

00:00:36.485 --> 00:00:40.135
A similarity needs both items, and what they share.

00:00:40.135 --> 00:00:43.510
A difference needs both items, and how they differ.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.185
For an unfamiliar audience, the answer must explain the unfamiliar thing.

00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:53.049
And aim means why, method means how, and finding means what they found.

00:00:54.081 --> 00:00:55.406
Let's try one.

00:00:55.406 --> 00:00:56.956
Read the goal first.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.931
Emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two spans.

00:00:59.931 --> 00:01:03.606
So the checklist is: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:03.606 --> 00:01:05.331
A states a similarity.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.686
B is a difference, but in dates.

00:01:07.686 --> 00:01:09.836
D only mentions one bridge.

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.696
C has two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:14.177
It ticks every box.

00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:18.464
Watch out for the true sentence that does a different job.

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:20.214
Every choice is accurate.

00:01:20.214 --> 00:01:21.788
Only one hits the goal.

00:01:22.844 --> 00:01:24.744
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:25.819
How to spot it.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.194
The four steps.

00:01:27.194 --> 00:01:28.439
The goal words.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:29.464
And the trap.

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:32.227
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
